# README — Source Data: Volcano Plots and Reactome GSEA

## Overview
This file contains the differential expression results and Reactome gene set
enrichment analysis (GSEA) results underlying the volcano plots and GSEA dot
plots shown for each pairwise endotype comparison (All Low vs Mixed, Mixed vs
All High, All Low vs All High) in the 2000HIV cohort (NCT03994835).

## Sheets
Nine sheets are included, three per comparison:

| Sheet name | Panel | Comparison | Content |
|---|---|---|---|
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_Volcano_Discovery | a (left) | All Low vs Mixed | Discovery cohort DE results |
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_Volcano_Validation | a (middle) | All Low vs Mixed | Validation cohort DE results |
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_GSEA_Reactome_Discovery | a (right) | All Low vs Mixed | Reactome GSEA (Discovery only) |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_Volcano_Discovery | b (left) | Mixed vs All High | Discovery cohort DE results |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_Volcano_Validation | b (middle) | Mixed vs All High | Validation cohort DE results |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_GSEA_Reactome_Discovery | b (right) | Mixed vs All High | Reactome GSEA (Discovery only) |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_Volcano_Discovery | c (left) | All Low vs All High | Discovery cohort DE results |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_Volcano_Validation | c (middle) | All Low vs All High | Validation cohort DE results |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_GSEA_Reactome_Discovery | c (right) | All Low vs All High | Reactome GSEA (Discovery only) |

## Column definitions

### Volcano sheets (*_Volcano_Discovery / *_Volcano_Validation)
One row per gene tested in the corresponding DESeq2 differential expression
model.

- **GENEID:** Ensembl gene ID (versioned).
- **SYMBOL:** HGNC gene symbol.
- **GENETYPE:** gene biotype (e.g., protein_coding).
- **DESCRIPTION:** gene description.
- **CHR:** chromosome.
- **comparison:** the pairwise comparison this row belongs to.
- **regulation:** significance/direction flag assigned during the DESeq2
  pipeline (n.s. / up / down). 
- **baseMean:** mean of normalized counts across all samples (DESeq2 output).
- **log2FoldChange:** log2 fold change between groups. This is the x-axis
  value in the volcano plot.
- **lfcSE:** standard error of the log2 fold change.
- **pvalue:** raw p-value from the DESeq2 Wald test.
- **padj:** Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value. This is the y-axis value
  (as -log10(padj)) in the Discovery volcano plot; the Validation volcano
  plot instead uses -log10(pvalue) (raw p-value), consistent with the
  discovery/validation two-stage design.


### GSEA sheets (*_GSEA_Reactome_Discovery)
One row per Reactome pathway tested by `gsePathway()` (all pathways passing
the pipeline's internal significance cutoff, not just those shown in the
dot plot), computed on the Discovery cohort only. Sorted by `p.adjust`
ascending. The dot plot itself shows only a subset of these rows — the top
15 most positive and top 15 most negative NES pathways with p.adjust < 0.05.

- **ID:** Reactome pathway identifier.
- **Description:** pathway name (as labeled in the plot).
- **setSize:** number of genes in the pathway gene set. This is the point
  size in the plot.
- **enrichmentScore:** raw (non-normalized) GSEA enrichment score.
- **NES:** normalized enrichment score, adjusted for gene set size. This is
  the x-axis value in the plot.
- **pvalue:** raw GSEA p-value.
- **p.adjust:** Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value. -log10(p.adjust) is
  the color scale in the plot.
- **qvalue:** Storey's q-value, an alternative FDR estimate to p.adjust.
- **rank:** position in the ranked gene list at which the running
  enrichment score reached its maximum (the leading-edge peak).
- **leading_edge:** summary statistics for the leading-edge subset —
  `tags` (% of gene set members contributing to the enrichment signal),
  `list` (% of the ranked list scanned to reach the peak), and `signal`
  (combined enrichment signal strength).
- **genes:** leading-edge genes (gene symbols) driving the enrichment
  signal for that pathway, semicolon-separated.

## Data processing
- Differential expression was performed using DESeq2, adjusted for Age, Sex,
  Season of Collection, Plate (batch effects), Genetic PC1, COVID
  vaccination, and Time to Laboratory Processing (Discovery cohort model
  additionally adjusts for Center).
- Discovery and Validation cohort models were run independently on the same
  gene set.
- GSEA gene ranking used -log10(raw p-value) x sign(log2FoldChange), based
  on genes with a mapped Entrez ID; for Entrez IDs mapping to multiple
  Ensembl IDs, the ID with the most extreme ranking value was retained.
- GSEA was performed using the Reactome pathway database (ReactomePA::
  gsePathway), Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction, minimum gene set size 10,
  maximum gene set size 500. Only the Discovery cohort was used for GSEA, as
  it is the larger of the two cohorts.
- The plotted GSEA pathways are restricted to the top 15 (by NES, in each
  direction) among pathways passing p.adjust < 0.05; this is the same subset
  reported in these sheets.

## Relationship to other source data
Sample-level cluster/endotype assignments used to define comparison groups
are provided in the Endotype_Label sheet of the multi-omics heatmap source
data file. Raw bulk RNA-seq data are deposited in the Radboud Data Repository
(RDR); see the manuscript's Data Availability statement for repository links.

